 "verdict": "SIGN FLIP ON THE PLANCHEREL ARM \u2014 P(A=3) is POSITIVE while P(A=2) was NEGATIVE. The 2nd-order Magnus pairing weighted by the quantum Plancherel measure d_q(\u03bb)\u00b2/[n]_q! REVERSES sign between the deuteron (A=2) and the triton (A=3), the signature the merged Magnus-wall audit named for a correction that reduces binding at A=2 and adds it at A\u22653. \u26a0 THE HEADLINE ARM DISAGREES. Under the production Wenzl/Markov weight \u2014 the one `headline_pairing` declares, and the one every other tr_M in the corpus uses \u2014 P(A=3) is negative and P(A=2) was negative, i.e. NO flip. So this verdict is a statement about the Plancherel arm ONLY. Reporting it as the result, when the measure that yields it was not chosen on principle, would be selection against the target (AGENTS.md). Which measure is correct is bean qou-za3q decision 1, still OPEN. Control tr_M(\u03a9\u2082)=0 holds (weight-independently); per-partition sign-indefinite (14+/14-). HONEST LIMITS: dimensionless SIGN datum only (scope-a); NOT a MeV (open \u0394_\u03bb gate), NOT a physical binding-sign assertion (that is qou-v7ro/#6077, cited not re-derived). Mapping any of it to 'binding' still needs the sign convention.",
 "scope": "scope-(a): decides the A=3 SIGN of tr_M(\u03c1\u00b7\u03a9\u2082) and its relation to the A=2 sign. Dimensionless structural datum. Does NOT reproduce any MeV (open \u0394_\u03bb gate \u2014 a number would be a fit). Does NOT assert a physical binding-sign convention (qou-v7ro / PR #6077, cited not re-derived). No fit; nothing inverted; nothing wired.",
